        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   The Trion BBS system has an integrated Questionair system.
   The system consists of a door to ask the Questions, a door
   to view questions in the online UserEditors and a build in
   view methode in the offline GUI usereditor.

   The door to ask the questions is called DoQuest and should
   be run in the start menu when users of all levels log in.

   Add something like this do the start.src menu.

   CliDoor     "doors:quest/DoQuest ~50 ~51"

   The door is started at every login, but only appears to
   users when there are unanswered questions.
   This way the sysop can add questions later, and all
   users will be asked to answer the new question.

   Als the Sysop can delete answers to questions if he is not
   satisfied with the answer .. the user has to answer that
   question again when he logs in later.


   To view a questionair there is a 'ViewQuest' door wich will
   be started if the 'I' is pressed in the online user editors.
   Also you can use this door too view the Questionair from the
   user online by adding the folowing to a menu:

   CliDoor     "doors:quest/ViewQuest ~50 ~51"


   The Questionair system uses the "trion:cfg/questionair.cfg"
   configuration file to know what the questions are.








       Example Questionair configuration file

;
;Examples  (2 types possible, Multiple choice And text)
;
;Note , QuestionID is a Unique number so you can add questions later
;       and only the unanswered questions will be asked.
;       Start a question with a QuestionID: line and end it with the
;       Question: line.
;
;QuestionID:  1          ;(1-255) 
;Type:        Multi      ;field optional, options (text,multi), default: text
;Options:     3          ;field optional, default: 2
;Question:
;Are you male or female ?
;Male
;Female
;I Dunno
;
;
;QuestionID:  2          ;(1-255) 
;Type:        Text       ;field optional, options (text,multi), default: text
;Mandatory               ;field optional, Users have to answer with this.
;Lines:       4          ;field optional, default: 1
;Question:
;Tell me about your computer equipment ?
;





QuestionID:  1
Type:        Text
Mandatory
Lines:       1
Question:
When were you born ?



QuestionID:  2
Type:        Multi
Options:     3
Question:
Are you male or female ?
Male
Female
I Dunno



QuestionID:  3
Type:        Text
Mandatory
Lines:       4
Question:
Tell me about your computer equipment (4 lines) ?



